he8|n|One who cuts; as, a stone cutter; a die cutter; esp., one who cuts out garments. ; That which cuts; a machine or part of a machine, or a tool or instrument used for cutting, as that part of a mower which severs the stalk, or as a paper cutter. ; A fore tooth; an incisor. ; A boat used by ships of war. ; A fast sailing vessel with one mast, rigged in most essentials like a sloop. A cutter is narrower end deeper than a sloop of the same length, and depends for stability on a deep keel, often heavily weighted with lead. ; A small armed vessel, usually a steamer, in the revenue marine service; -- also called revenue cutter. ; A small, light one-horse sleigh. ; An officer in the exchequer who notes by cutting on the tallies the sums paid. ; A ruffian; a bravo; a destroyer. ; A kind of soft yellow brick, used for facework; -- so called from the facility with which it can be cut.	a:w58,140,2;245t,89,4;1j2g,51,3;8gk,46,2;1m36,34,4;8ul,20,2~245t,89,4;1m36,34,4;1j2g,51,3;w58,140,2;8gk,46,2;8ul,20,2	v:qtk,45,2~qtk,45,2	V:804,38,1~804,38,1	n:w58,130,1;fjk,122,64;27et,116,9;yis,80,5;yli,71,6;1w9l,70,3;164s,69,11;1j2g,63,7;28y5,59,9;1wyo,52,3;8gk,52,3;9xj,42,9;2223,35,3;8ul,30,4;1ukf,22,4~fjk,122,64;164s,69,11;28y5,59,9;9xj,42,9;27et,116,9;1j2g,63,7;yli,71,6;yis,80,5;8ul,30,4;1ukf,22,4;arv,21,4;2223,35,3;1wyo,52,3;1w9l,70,3;8gk,52,3	N:13v8,121,3;1jm3,90,4;804,38,1;1u21,29,1;22p9,6,1~1jm3,90,4;13v8,121,3;1u21,29,1;804,38,1;22p9,6,1
